    "title": "Gunshot detection system alerted police to Kansas homicide - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Wichita\nGunshot detection system alerted police to Kansas homicide\n15 hours ago\nSEDGWICK COUNTY —Law enforcement are investigating another homicide in Wichita. Just before 1:30 a.m. Tuesday, police patrolling near the 600 block of N. Poplar in Wichita heard multiple gunshots. At the same time, a Raven gunshot detection alert was activated for the area, followed by several 911 calls reporting the shooting at 1:28 a.m., according to a media release from Wichita Police.",
